#subtitle: Building relations with the other Martian political parties.

= Inter-Party Relationships

The {!<span style="color: #ED7158;"><strong>SPM</strong></span>!} cannot, and should not, govern alone; we require the backing of other parties to achieve the democratic compromises Martians deserve. We can expand our reach by reinforcing ties with historic allies, opening dialogues with minor factions, or determining that it is wiser to stand on our own for now.

- @liberals: Strengthen our bonds with the {!<span style="color: #D3C24D;"><strong>Martian National Liberal Party</strong></span>!}, our historic ally.
- @left: Work toward repairing relationships with the {!<span style="color: #540808;"><strong>People's Liberation Front for Mars</strong></span>!}.
- @right: Reach out to the {!<span style="color: #5C3F1A;"><strong>Front for Mars</strong></span>!}...
- @futurist: Work with {!<span style="color: #12DB95;"><strong>Phobos</strong></span>!}.
- @spm_alone: Stand alone for now.
- @easy_discard

@liberals
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; mnlp_relation += 5*(1 - dissent)

As an historic ally and the only other major Marsist party, the {!<span style="color: #D3C24D;"><strong>Martian National Liberal Party</strong></span>!} is a natural partner for cooperation.

@left
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; plfm_relation += 5*(1 - dissent); reformist_dissent += 5

While the {!<span style="color: #540808;"><strong>People's Liberation Front for Mars</strong></span>!} views us as a moderate partner, and its radical fringes fear having their platform diluted, most of the party considers our cooperation inevitable. The reformists are not happy at our choice of establishing dialogue with such a party. 

@right
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; ffm_relation += 5*(1 - dissent); left_dissent += 8; romanticist_dissent += 8; reformist_dissent += 4; progressist_dissent += 4

The {!<span style="color: #5C3F1A;"><strong>Front for Mars</strong></span>!} is a fascist organization, and the mere thought of working with them has sparked widespread outrage across our base. Nonetheless, both parties share overlapping roots in syndicalism and Marsist rhetoric.

@futurist
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; p_relation += 5*(1 - dissent)

{!<span style="color: #12DB95;"><strong>Phobos</strong></span>!} remains an enigmatic party, yet they still identify as Marsists. Perhaps closer alignment will secure us a useful ally.

@spm_alone

Whether by choice or circumstance, we refrain from forming new political ties at this time.

- @return: Continue...
